{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4387284","formula":"C₂₆H₅₀O₄","hill":"C26H50O4","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":26.0,"H":50.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Diethylhexyl sebacate","ru":"Диоктилсебацинат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dioctyl sebacate (also di(2-ethylhexyl) sebacate, commonly abbreviated as DOS, DEHS, and BEHS) is an organic compound which is the diester of sebacic acid and 2-ethylhexanol. It is an oily colorless liquid and is used as a plasticizer, including in the explosive C-4. It has also found use in Dot 5 brake fluid, in ester-based engine oils and additives, as seed particle for particle image velocimetry (PIV) and as a model compound that forms stable aerosols.","ru":"Диоктилсебацинат (ДОС) представляет собой прозрачную (с желтизной) жидкость с плохо различимым фруктовым запахом. Диоктилсебцинат получают из себациновой кислоты, которая, в свою очередь, производится из перегретого касторового масла. Диоктилсебацинат является сложным эфиром себациновой кислоты."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":31218,"mass":426.7,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCC(CC)COC(=O)CCCCCCCCC(=O)OCC(CC)CCCC","inchikey":"VJHINFRRDQUWOJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"bis(2-ethylhexyl) decanedioate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"31218","atoms":80,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":9.549,"y":-0.605,"z":-1.807,"el":"C"},{"x":9.183,"y":0.061,"z":-0.488,"el":"C"},{"x":8.638,"y":-0.92,"z":0.55,"el":"C"},{"x":7.239,"y":-1.487,"z":0.268,"el":"C"},{"x":5.995,"y":-0.604,"z":0.551,"el":"C"},{"x":5.167,"y":-0.307,"z":-0.721,"el":"C"},{"x":5.793,"y":0.666,"z":-1.705,"el":"C"},{"x":6.249,"y":0.64,"z":1.419,"el":"C"},{"x":5.024,"y":1.352,"z":1.673,"el":"O"},{"x":4.293,"y":0.922,"z":2.738,"el":"C"},{"x":4.609,"y":0.014,"z":3.493,"el":"O"},{"x":3.04,"y":1.756,"z":2.865,"el":"C"}